{title: 614 - Sound the Battle Cry}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #614 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 614}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Ab]Sound the battle cry, [Db]See! the [Ab]foe is nigh;
[Eb]Raise [Ab]the [Eb]standard high [Bb7]For the [Eb]Lord;
[Ab]Gird your armor on, [Db]Stand firm, [Ab]every one,
Rest your [Fm]cause upon His [Ab]ho[Eb7]ly[Ab]word.
[Ab]Rouse, then soldiers! [Eb7]rally round the [Ab]banner!
[C]Ready, [Fm]steady, [Bb7]pass the word a[Eb]long;
[Ab]Onward, forward, [Eb7]shout aloud ho[Ab]sanna!
[Ab]Christ is [Fm]Captain of the [Ab]might[Eb7]y[Ab]throng.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[Ab]Rouse, [Db]then [Ab]soldiers!
[Eb][Ab]rally [Eb]round [Bb7]the [Eb]banner!
[Ab]Ready, steady, [Db]pass the [Ab]word along;
[Fm]Onward, [Ab]forward, [Eb7]shout [Ab]aloud hosanna!
[Ab]Christ is [Eb7]Captain of [Ab]the mighty throng.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Ab]Strong [Db]to meet [Ab]the foe,
[Eb][Ab]Marching [Eb]on [Bb7]we [Eb]go,
[Ab]While [Db]our cause [Ab]we know
[Fm][Ab]Must [Eb7][Ab]prevail;
[Ab]Shield [Eb7]and [Ab]banner bright,
[C]Gleaming [Fm]in [Bb7]the [Eb]light,
[Ab]Battling [Eb7]for [Ab]the right,
[Ab][Fm]We [Ab]ne'er [Eb7]can [Ab]fail.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Ab]O [Db]Thou God [Ab]of all,
[Eb]Hear [Ab]us [Eb]when [Bb7]we [Eb]call,
[Ab]Help [Db]us, one [Ab]and all,
[Fm][Ab]By [Eb7]Thy [Ab]grace;
[Ab]When [Eb7]the [Ab]battle's done,
[C]And [Fm]the [Bb7]victory [Eb]won,
[Ab]May [Eb7]we wear [Ab]the crown
[Ab][Fm]Before [Ab][Eb7]Thy [Ab]face.
{end_of_verse}
